# Build context uploaded by `gcloud run jobs deploy --source=.`
# (infra/builder-job.deploy.sh).
#
# Without this file gcloud uploads the entire working tree (gigabytes, with
# node_modules, tmp/ and worktrees), which stalls the deploy long before
# Cloud Build ever starts. Note that
# .dockerignore does NOT help: it is applied by the builder, after the upload.
#
# Keep in mind these are different filters with different jobs:
#   .gcloudignore  — what gets UPLOADED to Cloud Build
#   .dockerignore  — what gets into the IMAGE from what was uploaded
# Anything the Dockerfile COPYs must survive both. Today that is services/,
# taxonomy/ and agent/skills/check.py.

.git/
.github/
.claude/

# Local Python env + caches — never a build input.
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Local scanner artifacts (data/downloads, scanner.db) and scratch space
# (tmp/authoring/ holds raw dataset rows from local recipe authoring).
data/
tmp/

# Legacy model-eval snapshots (retired agent builder): local-only and
# gitignored because agent output embeds raw dataset content including
# personal contact details. The builder
# Dockerfile COPYs services/page_builder wholesale, so without this line
# (and the matching one in .dockerignore) every --source deploy would bake
# that PII into the image.
services/page_builder/harness-comparison/

# Only the two `--source=.` deploys read this file, and both build the root
# Dockerfile, which COPYs nothing from frontend/. The Cloud Build triggers
# (cloudbuild-publish.yaml, cloudbuild-publisher-image.yaml) clone the repo
# and never see this file. frontend/ SOURCE is still uploaded (about 1MB) so
# a hand-run `gcloud builds submit` of either config keeps working. What is
# dropped below is generated or downloaded locally and gitignored, so no
# build reads it from the checkout: the publish steps fetch or write it.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.output/
frontend/.nuxt/
node_modules/
# Vite dep cache (vite.cacheDir).
frontend/.cache/
# Symlink to .output/public. No trailing slash, so the link itself matches.
frontend/dist
# Written by the publisher, copy-libs.mjs and the GCS rsync at publish time.
frontend/public/data/
frontend/public/datasets/
frontend/public/lib/
frontend/public/news/

# Recipes are read from git main at run time (RECIPES_SOURCE), and no
# Dockerfile COPYs recipes/ (about 19MB of the upload before this line).
recipes/
# Docs and lint cache: not build inputs.
docs/
.ruff_cache/

.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.DS_Store
*.db

# Untracked local working dirs (screen recordings, browser-automation
# screenshots, tool scratch, Firebase CLI cache). Never build inputs, and
# screenshots of dataset pages can carry the same PII as the eval snapshots.
motion/
.playwright-mcp/
.superpowers/
.firebase/

# Credentials must never ride along in an upload.
*.pem
*.key
*-sa.json
*credentials*.json
service-account*.json
